# PORTED.sha256 — port parity manifest (plan D24).
# SHA-256 over LF-NORMALIZED content, so it holds on Windows and Linux alike.
# Canonical source: schemas/blueprint/.shared/ in the Archally monorepo.
# Regenerate with: node scripts/port-parity.mjs --emit
#
# The `job` lines below tell the public-side verifier where each manifest prefix lives,
# relative to tools/. They are DATA, not decoration: without them the verifier would need a
# hand-maintained copy of this job list, and adding a job here while forgetting it there
# reports every file of the new job as 'missing from disk'. (Observed, 2026-07-26.)
# job quality-gate tools/quality-gate
# job semantic-rules tools/semantic-checker/rules extras-ok
# job next-id tools/next-id
# job build-stamp tools/build-stamp
# job coverage-check tools/coverage-check
# job contract-surface tools/contract-surface extras-ok
# job entity-query tools/entity-query
# job doc-snippet-validate tools/doc-snippet-validate
# job validator tools/validator/src extras-ok
# job model-builder tools/model-builder/src extras-ok
# job schema-update tools/schema-update/src extras-ok
# job renderer tools/renderer/src extras-ok
# job port tools/port
# job vscode-blueprint-navigation tools/vscode-blueprint extras-ok
# job example-prestashop examples/prestashop/.blueprint/v2.8 extras-ok

